## THE ANSWER YOU BUILD (the coordinator's, recorded; NOT the product owner's, who may overrule it)
Jira MPSCALC-365 comment 40682 (read at drafting, GET): "a device line of quantity zero does not count as a counted device line, because it carries no devices. The filter of the counted set gains a quantity above zero; the zero line itself stays listed and flagged as zero per device." Row wanted: "a section with a device line of twelve, a device line of zero and a care pack of twenty-four, expecting the care pack flagged at two per device; it must fail when the filter is removed." Also at `1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md:2426` (item 6 of the batch-11 section). Ticket Done-when (Acceptance check, read at drafting): "The answer is recorded; one committed row with a device line of quantity 0 expects it and fails when the rule is flipped the other way." The answer part is MET; your branch supplies the row and the filter.

